    "notes":  [
                  "Earlier live-text failures exposed stale-field input intent and loss of multi-selection during complete double-click sequences. The final canvas-text flow covers both fixes.",
                  "A canvas regression started while geometry dependencies were being extracted loaded a mixture of old HTML and new scripts in nested frames. Its incomplete 459-pass/1-failure result was superseded on frozen product source. Subsequent fixture updates open the collapsed Look section and verify preserved free geometry; component reruns account for the complete canvas suite without double counting.",
                  "The table choice test now waits for observable keyboard navigation after a grid rebuild instead of assuming it completes within 150 ms. Its exact data and navigation assertion is unchanged.",
                  "The narrow design flow exposed an inaccessible Paragraph control. Final alternate runs include its responsive-toolbar fix.",
                  "The current prose/field editor contrast and scope labels supersede the usability issues recorded in the earlier source-blind audit.",
                  "Pending-edit tests seed historical records to exercise date confirmation; ordinary chart-authoring acceptance flows create their charts and records through the GUI.",
                  "These results do not establish trusted hardware-input behavior, complete PowerPoint feature parity, or a human task-time comparison."
              ],
